{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms","id":1374641,"title":"Area-of-Effect solar charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-13T15:37:30-07:00","id":1374641,"title":"Area-of-Effect solar charms?","content":"I've been reading Gosu (The Master), and trying to write out a fiction where a Solar takes on a draka-esque empire. The thing is, is that the solar is going to have to kill each person individually, or at least kill thousand-man armies by the dozens at a time. <br /> <br /> Is there space for, say, Solar unleashing wide-area energy blasts like this: <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3.mkklcdnv3.com/mangakakalot/g2/gosu/chapter_30_the_baekma_valley_11/31.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Or is it too out of theme space? Would such a power fit inside a solar theme set, or is it more suited for martial arts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:04:18-07:00","id":1374645,"title":"","content":"That's sorcery. Rain of Doom is custom made for wiping out empires a city at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:04:25-07:00","id":1374646,"title":"","content":"Not really for Solar charms, that's a thing Dragonblooded and sorcerers do. It could be an Essence 5 capstone charm for a martial art revolving around energy manipulation or something though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:22:16-07:00","id":1374649,"title":"","content":"It could possibly be an artifact\u2019s Evocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T16:42:12-07:00","id":1374654,"title":"","content":"Charms in Miracles of the Solar Exalted go there somewhat. Brawl can annihilate everything within short range with Burning Sky Apocalypse Strike, and Archery has Solar Judgement Flare, which, <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/aXxiFqI\" target=\"_blank\">well...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T19:00:13-07:00","id":1374685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374654#post1374654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charms in Miracles of the Solar Exalted go there somewhat. Brawl can annihilate everything within short range with Burning Sky Apocalypse Strike, and Archery has Solar Judgement Flare, which, <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/aXxiFqI\" target=\"_blank\">well...</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder who's the unlucky sap right at ground zero of that attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T19:47:38-07:00","id":1374693,"title":"","content":"Cascade of Cutting Terror occupies a strange space here. It does incredible AOE damage to scenery and <i>trivial</i> opponents near your target, but doesn't actually harm more than one significant target...<br /> <br /> ... but! Now we have the spell Thorn of Cold Rebuke. The combination of the two should be suitably awe-inspiring.<br /> <br /> Also, as a general guideline, you can stunt your attacks however you feel is appropriate, and large groups of opponents (battle groups) can suffer large losses in what is systematically a single target attack. Thunderbolt Attack Prana does disgusting things to most BGs out of the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T20:05:07-07:00","id":1374697,"title":"","content":"Yeah if you want a sandstorm wind attack can easily slay 100 people at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T21:47:09-07:00","id":1374701,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have to confess to some confusion about <i>why</i> the Solar has to kill each person individually, and can\u2019t just throw one guy into a crowd of guys hard enough for both to get annihilated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T22:15:18-07:00","id":1374708,"title":"","content":"The pic in the OP looks more Nine Aeons Thew to me than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T02:39:15-07:00","id":1374727,"title":"","content":"Sorcery has you covered.<br /> <br /> Total Annihilation<br /> Rain of Doom<br /> Death Ray","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T09:52:29-07:00","id":1374769,"title":"","content":"As noted, Solar Charms <i>can</i> produce AoE effects, but this generally involves high-end Charms. Solars can produce explosions of sunfire, but not casually. You could certainly make custom Charms for the Abilities that don't already have something like that, but it would still be the kind of thing that requires you to build up a lot of Initiative and spend a bunch of motes.<br /> <br /> If killing thousand-man armies by the dozens seems impractical, it's plausible to develop War Charms that make it easier for the Solar to fight against battle groups, so you can kill them by the hundreds instead! (You wouldn't want to step on the toes of White Reaper Style too much, since that's its thing, but there's probably an appropriate way to do this.)<br /> <br /> ...But yeah, sorcery does this sort of thing a lot more naturally than Solar Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T16:49:54-07:00","id":1374829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms#post1374641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading Gosu (The Master), and trying to write out a fiction where a Solar takes on a draka-esque empire. The thing is, is that the solar is going to have to kill each person individually, or at least kill thousand-man armies by the dozens at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they're not. Do it like a commando unit, or other form of insurgency.<br /> <br /> There's some area for big blasts, but not like Dragon Ball Z level. Not the kind of thing that creates redundancy for the warstriders and the skyships and the Stormcallers. Solars as fighters lean more in the direction of the highly competent warrior.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T17:07:56-07:00","id":1374833,"title":"","content":"There's a Melee charm in Miracles that let's you deflect attacks into a shattering wave of destruction. There's Evocations. By definition anything you do to a battlegroup is gonna be slaying 5 men in a single cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T17:12:49-07:00","id":1374836,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be the point of a battlegroup? I mean one enemy mechanically that gets a box or two ticked off, but in the flavor the solar just freaking grabs the dude at the head and throws them back through the ranks so hard anyone who wasn't able to get out the way became part of a very unhappy and broken improvised wall slowing that first person down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T17:39:51-07:00","id":1374839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374654#post1374654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl can annihilate everything within short range with Burning Sky Apocalypse Strike</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that short range is about the size of a small room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T03:26:23-07:00","id":1374899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374769#post1374769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If killing thousand-man armies by the dozens seems impractical, it's plausible to develop War Charms that make it easier for the Solar to fight against battle groups, so you can kill them by the hundreds instead! (You wouldn't want to step on the toes of White Reaper Style too much, since that's its thing, but there's probably an appropriate way to do this.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest... for Solars with a lot of combat charms, it's pretty easy to kill <i>hundreds</i> of ordinary soldiers per hit when fighting battle groups. Killing a dozen or two is how I narrate it when a Solar hits a Size 5 Battle Group and does no damage (they killed some, but not enough to make a real dent in the opposing army).<br /> A Solar can potentially kill 1000 within 5 seconds with a really good roll, especially if they're not well-armoured (though I'd be more likely to narrate it as killing hundreds and then hundreds fleeing). You don't really need much in the way of special anti-Battle Group charms, just high withering damage will do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, in 2e Solar War didn't really have charms for being really good at slaughtering armies by yourself, it was more about tactics and command. Whereas 2e Abyssal War did.<br /> I wouldn't be shocked if that difference is maintained in 3rd ed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T05:13:19-07:00","id":1374903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374899#post1374899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest... for Solars with a lot of combat charms, it's pretty easy to kill <i>hundreds</i> of ordinary soldiers per hit when fighting battle groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook has a whole section describing what Magnitude damage actually translates into in-character and how it doesn't particularly correspond to actually killing the majority of combatants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s important to understand what Magnitude damage represents. Partially, it means dead or unconscious fighters, but it also represents damage to the group\u2019s morale\u2014 having the allies on either side of you cut down tests a person\u2019s resolve to stand and keep fighting, despite the dangerous likelihood that you may be next; in fact, without your fellows-at-arms, you\u2019re more likely to be next. Thus, Magnitude damage is a mixture of incapacitated combatants and those who have lost the will to fight, or have stopped fighting effectively. </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you were killing hundreds per hit, how would the rally for numbers action work?<br /> <br /> Even within the scope of who is actually killed, I find it makes a lot more sense to presume that the attack roll translates to a series of blows in short order rather than catching several people in a single sweep of the daiklave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374899#post1374899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Incidentally, in 2e Solar War didn't really have charms for being really good at slaughtering armies by yourself, it was more about tactics and command. Whereas 2e Abyssal War did.</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I wouldn't be shocked if that difference is maintained in 3rd ed.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Considering what we've already gotten out of War and equivalent in Dragon Blooded and Lunars in contrast to their previous Editions, I certainly would be.<br /> <br /> It would be a tad redundant against what regular combat Abilities do against battle groups, wouldn't it? Not to mention the poor lookout for the Abyssal player who wants to actually command their own armies.<br /> <br /> No wonder that general character surrounded by zombies with the rose in the corebook looks so melancholy, nobody there is listening to him.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-15-2020, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T10:35:23-07:00","id":1374937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374899#post1374899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, in 2e Solar War didn't really have charms for being really good at slaughtering armies by yourself, it was more about tactics and command. Whereas 2e Abyssal War did.<br /> I wouldn't be shocked if that difference is maintained in 3rd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there was In Doubt of Legions Spirit (in the Scroll of Errata, DotFA section, replacing Immunity to Armies Approach). It was an Essence 6 War Charm that made it comically difficult for large armies to hit a Solar fighting as a solo unit.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Solars didn't have anything equivalent to Glorious Carnage Typhoon (which was damn near entry-level for Abyssals, requiring only a War Excellency).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T02:04:38-07:00","id":1375041,"title":"","content":"It bears noting that per the mechanics, the value of an area-of-effect attack against a battle group isn't necessarily in the damage, but in how it increases the difficulty of the roll they need to make to not rout completely when you deplete their Magnitude (pop pop).<br /> <br /> And when a battle group is at its largest size, you probably do want to rout it quickly, because the modifiers to its attacks and Defence are still high and its Initiative hasn't changed. I think it can be a bad idea to get into a protracted fight against a large battle group, especially if they've got a decent commander to further improve their rolls.<br /> <br /> Speaking of:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1374899#post1374899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar can potentially kill 1000 within 5 seconds with a really good roll, especially if they're not well-armoured (though I'd be more likely to narrate it as killing hundreds and then hundreds fleeing). You don't really need much in the way of special anti-Battle Group charms, just high withering damage will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that work with rout checks? What, do you let damage in excess of a battle group's Magnitude (pop pop) roll over into the next battle group if it holds together? How good is this roll, about fifty successes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T02:55:17-07:00","id":1375048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1374641-area-of-effect-solar-charms?p=1375041#post1375041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnitude (pop pop).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really taking me back. Now I've got to watch some more <i>Community</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T08:49:24-07:00","id":1375818,"title":"","content":"Large-scale annihilation is not outside of Solar thematics - but it's generally not a provice of combat charms, but rather of Sorcery, or Craft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T10:53:15-07:00","id":1375834,"title":"","content":"Waaait... why did I forget about God King's Shrike?<br /> <br /> Sure, it can't be deployed at will in the middle of a battle to catch up people bunched together, but it's well suited to reprimanding a state to which one objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}